text.section:
If the court determines that a fiduciary decision was an abuse of the fiduciary's discretion, the court may order a remedy authorized by law, including § 64.2-792. To place the beneficiaries in the positions the beneficiaries would have occupied if there had not been an abuse of the fiduciary's discretion, the court may order:

The fiduciary to exercise or refrain from exercising the power to adjust under § 64.2-1038;


The fiduciary to exercise or refrain from exercising the power to convert an income trust to a unitrust under subdivision A 1 of § 64.2-1041, change the percentage or method used to calculate a unitrust amount under subdivision A 2 of § 64.2-1041, or convert a unitrust to an income trust under subdivision A 3 of § 64.2-1041;


The fiduciary to distribute an amount to a beneficiary;


A beneficiary to return some or all of a distribution; or


The fiduciary to withhold an amount from one or more future distributions to a beneficiary.
